WEBVTT

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.410
Argent Point?

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.600
I didn't know there
was a base out here.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.710
It only started functioning recently.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.040
It exists solely to research
new Trail Krieger models.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.630
They're working hard
on that new model.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.030
Sure.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:35.930
If they can get it working, it'll change the course of the war.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.430
Maybe the war with Ingelmia
will end immediately.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.320
Or maybe we'll lose our jobs.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.810
Right...

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.540
Well, supposedly it's just that amazing.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:47.810
Right, General?

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:51.570
I'm a second lieutenant, Sergeant Quasimodo.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.400
Sergeant Major Suzushiro, tell them we'll be arriving soon.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:56.310
Yes, sir.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:07.560
Reika Nanjou

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.740
I'm Maeda, the man
in charge here.
Reika Nanjou

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.090
As you all know,
Reika Nanjou

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:16.340
the research being done at this
base is above top secret.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:23.640
In other words, your responsibility as the security team is of the utmost importance.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.000
You must be on the lookout for intelligence gathering attempts by foreign nations,

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.040
as well as direct assaults.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:34.860
Guarding the facilities, personnel, and everything on this base is your job.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.190
Keep that in mind—

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.940
Wh-What are you doing?

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:42.410
You can't just wander around in that!

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.290
I'm so glad there's a girl here.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:53.790
I'm Reika Nanjou.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:57.360
H-Hello... I'm Saori Suzushiro.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.670
This is Sub-lieutenant Nanjou, by the way.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.280
Keep that in mind!

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.830
I-I'm sorry!

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.680
Um...

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.430
I prefer handshakes.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:14.620
You're a very kind and honest person, aren't you, Suzushiro-san?

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.920
Nice to meet you.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.320
It's a pleasure.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.650
Nice to meet you, too!

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.350
Yes, nice to meet you!

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.630
Nice to meet you, Squad Leader.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:40.200
Second Lieutenant Ukyou Samonji, leader of Squad 37.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:41.670
I'll be in charge of security here.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.930
I'd like to shake your hand.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:49.550
I believe a salute is called for here.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.610
You're a mean person, Second Lieutenant Samonji.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.460
Man, this is hilarious.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:09.850
The general doesn't know what to do.

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.060
Huh? He's not mad?

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.950
He has no idea what to do.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.990
I haven't seen him like that in ages.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:18.860
Really?

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:26.640
What?

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.390
So you're the son of a rich financier, Quasimodo?

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.130
You don't look it at all!

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.840
Sorry I look poor.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.250
I didn't mean that...

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.220
Wait, maybe I did?

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:42.560
Well, it's my dad who's got the money, not me.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:44.780
And I've been disowned.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.810
Are you trying to get promoted to show him up?

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:47.790
No way.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.900
Suzushiro-chan will be bossing me around in five years.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.530
No way...

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:55.180
You're aiming for the top, Reika-chan?

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.060
You're already a lieutenant at your age.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:02.550
I only got this job because I was able to work with the new model's system...

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:06.380
But I'd want to be at the very top, I guess.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.230
Like a field marshal?

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:14.890
I want to become really important, and make an army where nobody dies.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:17.060
An army where nobody dies?

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.310
That's very philosophical.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.260
I think, given our present relationship with Ingelmia,

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.820
getting rid of our military isn't realistic.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:31.380
So I think we just need to make it so if war does break out, nobody dies.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.400
You're pretty funny, Reika-chan.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.830
Bizarre! That's great!

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.900
Is it that bizarre?

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.180
Hey, General.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.840
Reika-chan says she's going to become field marshal and make an army where nobody dies.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.210
What will you do if that happens?

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.730
Nothing.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.350
Tell me.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:58.350
Tell me what you think, Samonji-san.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:01.620
I've already told you.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:04.700
You think it's impossible, don't you?

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.740
I think it isn't even something that's worth discussing the possibility of.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.510
I know it sounds stupid,

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:16.360
but if we want to change things, isn't it necessary to have ideals?

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.750
Then I'll tell you.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:25.690
If you aren't willing to die, you can't be a soldier.

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:28.690
In other words, your ideals mean nothing in the military.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:32.420
There's a difference between dying and being willing to die.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.690
I don't want anybody to...

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.400
It's time to go on standby, isn't it?

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:43.480
Excuse me.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.820
Goodbye.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:10.270
Those three are unmanned.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:13.310
They're being controlled by Nanjou-kun's commander unit.

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.660
Remote controlled?

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.040
No, it's using what she's got up here.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:26.290
The unmanned units share experiences using the pilot's brain functions

00:06:26.290 --> 00:06:29.130
and automatically analyze the situation.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.550
It's a revolutionary system.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:34.660
In another six months, we'll have eight unmanned units.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:39.160
What about the physical stress it places on the pilot?

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:43.710
We had a lot of people who showed promise, but they all washed out.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.090
She's the last one.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.590
Don't touch me!

00:06:59.550 --> 00:06:59.570
Wait!

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:00.490
Reika-san!
Wait!

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.200
Let me go.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:37.740
I'm all right.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.720
Oh, good!

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.490
Lt. Nanjou, come this way.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:42.850
No!

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:49.860
Okay.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:50.890
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:52.340
I apologize.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.650
Sorry I'm late, since I was the one who asked you to come.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:41.240
It's a woman's prerogative to make men wait.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.010
I guess even you can tell jokes, Samonji-san.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:51.760
I'm embarrassed you saw that.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.890
Don't be. Are you all right?

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.970
It's not like that all the time.

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:02.730
I just get a little edgy after the experiments.

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:06.350
Today was worse than usual...

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:10.520
The children weren't doing what I told them to.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:13.520
The unmanned units?

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.860
It's an interesting system.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:21.530
It's like I'm sharing a little of my personality with lots of children.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:27.030
And the decisions they make and the things they do are fed back to me,

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:30.310
and then I give it back to the children...

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:34.180
And that's an army where no one dies?

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:35.100
Yes.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:38.550
If nothing else, I think it'll be needed for that.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:42.190
So what did you really want to talk about?

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:44.890
Huh? Um, well...

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:50.420
I never really know what you're thinking, Samonji-san.

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.460
Your expression doesn't really change.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:53.950
Is that what you wanted to talk about?

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:56.060
No, not that.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.390
That makes me happy...

00:10:00.390 --> 00:10:01.570
No, that's not right.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.080
It makes me feel at ease?

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.260
Like, no matter what's happening with me,

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:09.400
you'll always look at me in the same way...

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.420
So, well...

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:19.040
Will you watch me,

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.440
and make sure I don't change?

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:27.090
Guarding the test pilot is our most important mission.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:30.390
I've been doing that from the start,

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:32.390
and I'll do it as long as you want me to.

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:37.600
So, you can follow your ideals.

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:40.310
Just as you want to do.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.270
I had a baby!

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:22.690
A fifth unmanned unit?

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:26.150
Yeah. It's taken a little time since number four.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.030
Your ideals won't go anywhere.

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:31.500
Get closer to them little by little.

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:33.980
Right!

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:37.040
So, what are you naming this one?

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:39.240
The first was named after your little brother,

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:41.740
and the others are from historical novels, right?

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:43.340
Actually, I'm out of ideas.

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:46.430
Okay, I'll volunteer! What about my name?

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.210
Oh, I never thought of that!

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:49.560
Okay, I'll name it Saori.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:50.180
Wha...
Okay, I'll name it Saori.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.420
I'm sure it'll grow up to be a good, honest child.

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:53.020
I'm honored.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.090
Hello?

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:58.310
Well, if I name it Quasimodo, it'll probably grow up lazy.

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:00.780
Well, I can't deny that.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:01.650
Right?

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:04.310
So why not name the next one after me?

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:08.320
You don't want to give them all such formal names

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.040
and have them grow up to be boring, right?

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.330
Back then, Captain Samonji

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:16.870
had a more peaceful look on his face than I'd ever seen him with.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:24.960
If Nanjou-san had stayed with him,

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:28.530
I'm sure his life would've changed.

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:31.390
And yours would have, as well.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:34.680
But...

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:37.570
It came before that could happen.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:59.600
You're looking even more lax than usual.

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:03.500
It's fine to do a demonstration for the brass,

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:06.750
but why did it have to be the day after my night shift?

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:10.260
Good morning, everyone!

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:14.390
It's a lovely morning, isn't it, Quasimodo-san? Saori-chan?

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:17.890
What's gotten into you, on an important day like this?

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:21.670
I was craving some of the sour coffee they have here.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.390
I'll take a cup.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:29.650
Sub-lieutenant Nanjou,

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:30.850
come with me.

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:33.870
Um... Sorry about the coffee!

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:41.030
Um, Samonji-san...

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:43.860
You're supposed to be on standby before the demonstration.

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:47.670
I just wanted some coffee.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:49.680
You don't have to get so mad.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:52.950
Are you scared?

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:01.920
I'm a little nervous, maybe.

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:05.270
Is there something bothering you?

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:08.180
My physical and mental states are fine.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:11.210
I just wanted to see everyone.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:14.330
If you need me to, I can tell the major to delay it—

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:15.290
No!

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.950
I've finally made it here!

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:17.710
But...

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:19.000
If you do that,

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:22.360
I'll whisper mean things into your ear when you sleep for the rest of your life!

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:24.080
I mean it!

00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:43.350
I believe a salute is called for here.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:49.060
Watch me, like you always do.

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:52.110
Then I'll be able to stay the same.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.650
Okay, I'll be going!

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:20.430
What? What's going on?

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:21.970
The seven unmanned units are out of control!

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:24.600
The commander unit isn't responding!

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.990
We can't get into the system, either!

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:46.010
It's spreading to all the units.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:48.000
Some are heading outside the base!

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:51.130
Damn it!

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.120
You're just an engineer. Get out of here!

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:55.760
He's fired. I'll give the orders.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:57.750
Execute Plan C immediately!

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:00.640
What's going on?

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.640
Shouldn't we move command centers?

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:06.070
Send Quasimodo's Krieger to the front gate.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:07.740
Don't let the unmanned units outside.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.270
Roger. I'll tell him.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.800
Suzushiro, you try to get to Reika.

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:15.180
What? But...

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:17.540
We'll stop Reika ourselves!

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:20.540
Yes, sir.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.160
Hey, security!

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.410
We're moving command centers!

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.070
Send us somewhere appropriate.

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:25.320
What is the Krieger squad doing?

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:27.390
As long as we've got the data, the machines don't matter!

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:29.570
Stop them if you have to destroy the pilot, too!

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:31.800
Hey, don't just stand there, do your job!

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:40.780
If you have them attack her, I'll kill you!

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:43.330
Hey, you! What did you to do—

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.560
Somebody do something!

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.570
Reika, I'm coming for you.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:17:01.130
We can't tell you to overcome those feelings.

00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:05.660
But you need to decide what you'll do.

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:15.380
The captain's regrets will never disappear, either.

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:23.930
Tokimune Susumu's last name comes from his mother.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:27.010
It was written on his forms.

00:17:27.010 --> 00:17:31.410
I thought there must be some reason one of your men punched you.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:35.200
I can't believe it was Reika Nanjou, though.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:39.640
Brigadier General Cowen told you they were siblings, right?

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.870
Is that why you tried to get Tokimune Susumu

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:46.470
away from Argevollen by making him hit you?

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:52.940
You've never been very good with this stuff.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.970
We'll just say that even you have too much to drink sometimes.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:17:59.980
I arranged for the latest Trail Krieger

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:04.390
and personnel familiar with them to be sent to Unit 8.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:05.850
Look at the documents.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.100
Watch out for Brigadier General Cayenne.

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:18.730
I know.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:41.710
Hey, it's Tokimune.

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:43.090
That's right, they let him out today.

00:18:43.090 --> 00:18:45.670
No alcohol for him for a while.

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:48.890
Good thing he got off with time in the guardhouse, right, Jamie?

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:51.340
Jamie?

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:54.450
Oh, yeah, alcohol's scary stuff.

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:01.090
That's all. Take care of it.

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:02.610
Understood.

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:16.640
As of 1500 today, I've been released.

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.090
I see.

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:20.950
I'm terribly sorry.

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:27.490
New Trail Kriegers will be arriving soon.

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:29.870
Get the details from Sergeant Appleton.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:32.270
Yes, sir.

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:40.250
I'm sorry.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.610
I didn't mean to sound so arrogant.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:50.140
I'm the one who still can't make a decision.

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:04.260
Stupid thing!

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.550
You've got my name!

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:06.920
You're supposed to be lazy!

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:19.730
Stop it!

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:21.090
Let me through!

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:26.320
Nanjou-san! Nanjou-san!

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:27.690
Please, answer me!

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:31.160
Hurry...

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.230
Nanjou-san!

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:33.200
Stop me...

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.580
Now...

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:40.590
Stop me!

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:42.840
While...

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:44.840
While I'm still me!

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.210
Hurry!

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:06.240
What are you doing?

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:13.220
Wait!

